org/web/20211103234938/https://variety.com/2021/music/news/blake-slatkin-producer-lil-nas-x-kid-laroi-1235075810/|url-status=live}}</ref> Over a repeated [[Cell (music)|melodic cell]], Laroi and Bieber switch between [[head voice]] and [[chest voice]] on a [[minor sixth]].<ref name="CBC">{{cite web|url=https://www.cbc.ca/music/the-honest-guy-s-bittersweet-summertime-ode-and-4-more-songs-you-need-to-hear-this-week-1.6100411|title=The Honest Guy's bittersweet summertime ode, and 4 more songs you need to hear this week|date=14 July 2021|publisher=[[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation]]|access-date=15 July 2021|archive-date=23 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210723024353/https://www.cbc.ca/music/the-honest-guy-s-bittersweet-summertime-ode-and-4-more-songs-you-need-to-hear-this-week-1.6100411|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jon Caramanica]] of ''[[The New York Times]]'' described the track as a "hyper-slick" hybridisation of [[New wave music|new wave]] and [[pop-punk]].<ref name="NYT">{{cite web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/09/arts/music/playlist-justin-bieber-kid-laroi-maluma.html|title=The Kid Laroi and Justin Bieber's Bouncy Plea, and 14 More New Songs|last1=Pareles|first1=Jon|last2=Caramanica|first2=Jon|last3=Russonello|first3=Giovanni|date=9 July 2021|work=[[The New York Times]]|access-date=10 July 2021|archive-date=9 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210709205217/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/09/arts/music/playlist-justin-bieber-kid-laroi-maluma.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Some critics found similarities between it and the music from Bieber's sixth studio album, ''[[Justice (Justin Bieber album)|Justice]]'' (2021). Justin Curto from ''[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]'' compared the song's sound to ''Justice'' single "[[Hold On (Justin Bieber song)|Hold On]]" and album tracks "Die for You" and "Somebody".<ref name="The Inside Track"/><ref name="Vulture">{{cite web|url=https://www.vulture.com/2021/07/watch-justin-bieber-the-kid-la